<title>JAPAN: Electric utilities close lower in Tokyo.</title>
<headline>Electric utilities close lower in Tokyo.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Japan's electric utilities sector closed lower on Thursday on uncertainty about their future business performance due to the yen&quot;s weakness, brokers said.</p>
<p>Tokyo Electric Power Co Inc fell 60 yen to close at 2,130, below its previous low for the year of 2,190 marked on Wednesday. Kansai Electric Power Co Inc slid 50 yen to close at 2,050 yen, surpassing its previous low for the year of 2,100 yen marked on February 7.  </p>
<p>Brokers said the weaker yen was likely to increase utilities industry also clouded their future.</p>
</text>
